<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.7.4: Relate the Domain of a Function to Its Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01855</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.7.4: Relate the Domain of a Function to Its Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>01993d6c-3b2f-4374-816d-ab9e8782e686</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>This graph represents the revenue in dollars that a company expects if they sell their product for \(p\) dollars.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Graph of non linear function.&quot; height=&quot;196"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4b5d552eb1fbfb0822e47b7883a920ba6c68d147"/></media></figure></para>

<section class="check-understanding"><title>Cool Down Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="7df5f3e7-792b-4438-a54b-e9a7d2660cd7"><problem><para>
      <para>Based on this model, which price would generate more revenue for the company, \($5\) or \($17\)?</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>$5</para><para>
      <para>Incorrect. The correct answer is \($5\), as it would generate about \($3,700\) in revenue. Charging \($17\) would bring in about \($2,500\).</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="91a80edb-e118-490e-9da1-3a90f3dac2be"><problem><para>
      <para>At what price (in dollars) should the company sell their product if they wish to make as much revenue as possible?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>10</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(10\). Based on the graph, a price of \($10\) would bring in the most revenue.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>What is an appropriate domain for the function? Explain how you know.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
  <para>\(0 \leq p \leq 20\), because the price has to be non-negative, and the company would earn negative revenue if the price were more than \($20\).</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
</document>
